    "description": "In this video, learn how to make original Nestle toll house chocolate chip cookies. First, whisk together all-purpose flour, baking soda, and salt. Next, beat together butter, white and brown sugar, and vanilla extract until it’s creamy. Continue to beat while adding two eggs and gradually pouring the rest of the flour mixture in. Now that the dough is formed, add chopped nuts and semisweet chocolate chips before shaping the cookie dough into individual balls on a baking sheet. Bake at 375 degrees for around ten minutes and let the cookies cool for two minutes. Enjoy this classic and easy-to-make cookie recipe. ",
